          %title
          %p This page compiles material related to the book collection:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haynes+Miller"} Haynes Miller
                (ed.)
              %p
                %em Handbook of Homotopy Theory
              %p Chapman and Hall/CRC Press 2019
              %p 982 pages
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.routledge.com/Handbook-of-Homotopy-Theory/Miller/p/book/9780815369707"} ISBN:9780815369707
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9781351251624"} doi:10.1201/9781351251624
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~hrm/papers/handbook-toc.pdf"}> table of contents
                )
          %p
            on
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %h2#terminology Terminology
          %p
            The editor,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haynes+Miller"} Haynes Miller
          %blockquote
            %p
              This volume may be regarded as a successor to the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"}> Handbook of Algebraic Topology
              ”, edited by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+James"} Ioan James
              and published a quarter of a century ago. In calling it the “Handbook of Homotopy Theory”, I am recognizing that the discipline has expanded and deepened, and traditional questions of topology, as classically understood, are now only one of many distinct mathematical disciplines in which it has had a profound impact and which serve as sources of motivation for research directions within homotopy theory proper.
